From c6b88ef2849bbbcc9eaa63677a5db73dc40ed801 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Cursor Agent <cursoragent@cursor.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 05:07:45 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 02/20] feat(workflow): find runs by idempotency key prefix

Deployment runs are about to be keyed per generation, so one service
owns several runs over its lifetime. Deleting or redeploying a service
must find every run whose instance may still be up, not only the run
of the current key.

WorkflowRuntime gains a non-abstract find_runs(key_prefix) that, like
find_run, has no side effects and defaults to NotImplementedError, so
existing runtimes such as the Temporal plugin keep working. The local
runtime answers it from the store with a GLOB query: case-sensitive,
wildcards in the prefix are matched literally, and the literal prefix
lets SQLite use the idempotency_key index.
